{# The THIRD google.protobuf.Struct site in the generated CRDs, and the reason this
   module is not only about generic_oidc: `spec.spiffe.jwt.extra_claims` on
   WorkloadIdentity hits the exact same crdgen code path as must_match_fields
   (schemagen.go, the .google.protobuf.Struct case), so it was broken the same way and
   is fixed by the same one-line change.

   Its job here is a DIFFERENT-RESOURCE regression guard: if a future change reverts
   the Struct handling, or narrows the fix to provision tokens only, the nested check
   below breaks even though every generic_oidc check still passes. The flat claim
   alongside it guards the other direction — that whatever replaces the fix does not
   break the case that already worked.

   Storage round-trip only. Proving the nested claim reaches an ISSUED JWT-SVID would
   need a bot, a workload-identity-jwt output and a JWT decoder; the CRD schema is what
   is under test here, and it is fully exercised by "the API server stored the whole
   tree and the operator wrote it to Teleport intact".

   Only spec.spiffe.id is required (lib/services/workload_identity.go
   ValidateWorkloadIdentity), and creating the resource needs no enterprise license —
   the operator's editor role already grants workload_identity RW. #}
apiVersion: resources.teleport.dev/v1
kind: TeleportWorkloadIdentityV1
metadata:
  name: op-workload-identity
  namespace: teleport
spec:
  spiffe:
    id: /harness/op-workload-identity
    jwt:
      extra_claims:
        # flat: worked even with the old `additionalProperties: true` schema
        team: {{ wi_flat_value }}
        # nested: pruned by the old schema, preserved by the fixed one
        nested:
          deep: {{ wi_nested_value }}
